<translate>
<!--T:3-->
The '''TextExtracts''' extension provides an API which allows retrieval of plain-text or limited HTML (HTML with content for [<tvar name=url>https://github.com/wikimedia/mediawiki-extensions-TextExtracts/blob/master/extension.json#L51</tvar> some CSS classes] removed) extracts of page content.

==Installation== <!--T:5-->
</translate>
{{Bundled|1.34}}
{{ExtensionInstall|TextExtracts
|registration=1
|no-registration-version=1.26
}}

<translate>
==Configuration settings== <!--T:6-->

<!--T:24-->
* <tvar name=1><code>$wgExtractsRemoveClasses</code></tvar> is an array of <tvar name=2>&lt;tag>, &lt;tag>.class, .&lt;class>, #&lt;id></tvar> which will be excluded from extraction.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:28-->
*:For example, <tvar name=1><code>$wgExtractsRemoveClasses[] = 'dl';</code></tvar> removes indented text, often used for non-templated hatnotes that are not desired in summaries.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:29-->
*:<tvar name=1>[[phab:diffusion/ETEX/browse/master/extension.json$46|extension.json]]</tvar> defines the defaults, of which the class "noexcerpt" is one - this may be added to any template to exclude it.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:30-->
* <tvar name=1><code>$wgExtractsExtendOpenSearchXml</code></tvar> defines whether TextExtracts should provide its extracts to the <tvar name=2>[[Special:MyLanguage/Api:Opensearch|Opensearch]]</tvar> API module.</translate> <translate><!--T:52--> The default is <tvar name=3>{{phpi|false}}</tvar>.</translate>

<translate>
== API == <!--T:7-->
</translate>
{{API-head
|module=extracts
|version=
|prefix=ex
|rrights=None
|postonly=No
|description=<translate><!--T:26--> Returns plain-text or limited HTML extracts of the given pages</translate>
|query=yes
}}
{{Api help|query+extracts}}
{{ApiEx
| desc=<translate><!--T:25--> Another example</translate>
| p1=action=query
| p2=prop=extracts
| p3=exchars=100
| p4=explaintext
| p5=titles=Earth
| result=<syntaxhighlight lang="javascript">{
    "query": {
        "pages": {
            "9228": {
                "pageid": 9228,
                "ns": 0,
                "title": "Earth",
                "extract": "Earth, also called the world and, less frequently, Gaia, (or Terra in some works of science fiction)..."
            }
        }
    }
}</syntaxhighlight>
}}

<translate>
=== Caveats === <!--T:32-->

<!--T:33-->
There are various things to be aware of when using the API or software that uses the API e.g. <tvar name=1>{{ll|Extension:Popups}}</tvar>.

<!--T:34-->
* We do not recommend the usage of `exsentences`.</translate> <translate><!--T:35--> It does not work for HTML extracts and there are many edge cases for which it doesn't exist.</translate> <translate><!--T:36--> For example "Arm. gen. Ing. John Smith was a soldier." will be treated as 4 sentences.</translate> <translate><!--T:37--> We do not plan to fix this.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:38-->
* Inline images are stripped from the response (even in HTML mode). This means if you are using the <tvar name=1>{{ll|Extension:Math|Math}}</tvar> extension and using formulae in your lead section they may not appear in the summary output.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:39-->
* In HTML mode we cannot guarantee well formed HTML. Resulting HTML may be invalid or malformed.</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:40-->
* In plaintext mode:
</translate>
**<translate><!--T:41--> citations may not be stripped (see <tvar name=1>[[phab:T197266]]</tvar>)</translate>
**<translate><!--T:42--> if a paragraph ends with an HTML tag e.g. ref tag, new lines may be dropped (see <tvar name=1>[[phab:T201946]]</tvar>)</translate>
**<translate><!--T:43--> new lines may be dropped after lists <tvar name=1>[[phab:T208132]]</tvar></translate>
** <translate><!--T:50--> Articles must begin with the lead paragraph for an extract to be generated.</translate> <translate><!--T:51--> The use of any template, and/or unclosed or empty HTML element may result in no preview for the article.</translate> E.g. <nowiki>"<div></div>hello</nowiki>" will give an empty extract.

<translate>
== FAQ == <!--T:44-->

=== How can I remove content from a page preview/extract? === <!--T:45-->
</translate>
<translate><!--T:46--> TextExtracts will strip any element that is marked with the class <tvar name=1>{{inline-code|.noexcerpt}}</tvar>.</translate>
<translate><!--T:47--> This is provided by the <tvar name=1>{{inline-code|$wgExtractsRemoveClasses}}</tvar> configuration variable (which also defines {{<tvar name=2>tmpl|0={{Git file|file=extension.json|project=mediawiki/extensions/TextExtracts|action=|branch=|sha=5309ab92bdb5d8c36a472f5c8e5d421d7747edeb|line=42|text=$1}}</tvar>|some other excluded elements}}).</translate>

